{%- comment -%}
  A piece's status, as one word (D25): reserved, soon, sold, presale, sale, new, or nothing.
  The owner sets it with tags (Shopify → Products → the piece → Tags). A piece in stock with
  none of these tags is simply available (2026-11-09).
    reserved  tagged reserved: held for a client. Not for sale and not sold, so it stays off the
              Archive. Stock can stay at 1 (the bag will not check it out, snippets/bag-foot) or
              go to 0 for a firm hold; either way it reads Reserved. Remove the tag to sell it again.
    soon      tagged coming-soon: shown before its Edition, not yet for sale. Never counted as sold,
              so it stays off the Record. Keep its stock at 0 until it goes live, then remove the tag.
              Also a piece in stock without a price: it can't be sold at £0 (2026-11-09).
    sold      not available, and not reserved or coming soon.
    presale   in transit: tagged in-transit (or pre-sale, the older word) and in stock. For sale
              now, ships within settings.transit_days days. A coming-soon piece can be in transit
              too: it stays soon, and its page says it is on its way.
    sale      a compare-at price above the price.
    new       available, and published within settings.new_days days. 0 turns New off.
  Use: {%- capture s -%}{%- render 'status', p: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = ''
  if p.tags contains 'reserved'
    assign s = 'reserved'
  elsif p.tags contains 'coming-soon'
    assign s = 'soon'
  elsif p.available == false
    assign s = 'sold'
  elsif p.price == 0
    assign s = 'soon'
  elsif p.tags contains 'in-transit' or p.tags contains 'pre-sale'
    assign s = 'presale'
  elsif p.compare_at_price > p.price
    assign s = 'sale'
  elsif settings.new_days > 0 and p.published_at
    assign now_s = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign pub_s = p.published_at | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign age = now_s | minus: pub_s
    assign limit = settings.new_days | times: 86400
    if age < limit
      assign s = 'new'
    endif
  endif
  echo s
-%}
